<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρί-ηρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, as
		epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταῖρος,</span> perh. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>faithful, trusty</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγάλως τιμώμενοι κτλ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἑταῖρος,</span> in sg.,
			only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.266
			</span></i> : elsewh. always in heterocl. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίηρες ἑταῖροι,</span> acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίηρας ἑταίρους</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτάρους ἐρίηρας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.100
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.47
			</span></i>, etc.; parodied by <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				143
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίηρος ἀοιδός</span>
			<i>loyal</i> to his master's house, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.346
			</span></i>, al.</div>
